      "content": "\"Letting go\" doesn't mean giving up on surviving; it means stopping the relentless, agonizing effort to *be* something when you've been broken into dust. The world doesn't *force* you to hurt; you're just reacting to the unbearable reality you're trapped in. Peace isn't found by fighting the hunt; it's found by ceasing to run, by finding a way to just *stop* the pain.",
